<item>
  <title>Getting Started with QuantLib in Python</title>
  <link>https://christopher-mclaren.github.io/blog/posts/quantlib-intro/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 





<p><a href="https://www.quantlib.org/">QuantLib</a> is the most comprehensive open-source library for quantitative finance. It handles everything from date arithmetic to full term structure models and derivatives pricing. This post walks through the basics.</p>
<section id="setup" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="setup">Setup</h2>
<p>If you’re using the <code>fineng</code> conda environment:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb1" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode bash code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode bash"><span id="cb1-1"><span class="ex" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">conda</span> install <span class="at" style="color: #657422;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-c</span> conda-forge quantlib-python</span></code></pre></div></div>
<p>Then import:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb2" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb2-1"><span class="im" style="color: #00769E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">import</span> QuantLib <span class="im" style="color: #00769E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">as</span> ql</span>
<span id="cb2-2"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">print</span>(ql.__version__)</span></code></pre></div></div>
</section>
<section id="setting-the-evaluation-date" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="setting-the-evaluation-date">Setting the evaluation date</h2>
<p>QuantLib has a global evaluation date that anchors all calculations:</p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb3" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb3-1">today <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> ql.Date(<span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">14</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">3</span>, <span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">2026</span>)</span>
<span id="cb3-2">ql.Settings.instance().evaluationDate <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> today</span>
<span id="cb3-3"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">print</span>(<span class="ss" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">f"Evaluation date: </span><span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">{</span>today<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">}</span><span class="ss" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"</span>)</span></code></pre></div></div>
</section>
<section id="building-a-discount-curve" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="building-a-discount-curve">Building a discount curve</h2>
<p>A discount curve maps each future date to a discount factor <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?P(0,%20T)">, which represents the present value of 1 unit of currency received at time <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?T">.</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?P(0,%20T)%20=%20e%5E%7B-r(T)%20%5Ccdot%20T%7D"></p>
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode" id="cb4" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode python code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode python"><span id="cb4-1">dates <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> [</span>
<span id="cb4-2">    today,</span>
<span id="cb4-3">    today <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">+</span> ql.Period(<span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">6</span>, ql.Months),</span>
<span id="cb4-4">    today <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">+</span> ql.Period(<span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1</span>, ql.Years),</span>
<span id="cb4-5">    today <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">+</span> ql.Period(<span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">2</span>, ql.Years),</span>
<span id="cb4-6">    today <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">+</span> ql.Period(<span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">5</span>, ql.Years),</span>
<span id="cb4-7">    today <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">+</span> ql.Period(<span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">10</span>, ql.Years),</span>
<span id="cb4-8">]</span>
<span id="cb4-9"></span>
<span id="cb4-10">discounts <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> [<span class="fl" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1.0</span>, <span class="fl" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0.978</span>, <span class="fl" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0.955</span>, <span class="fl" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0.910</span>, <span class="fl" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0.820</span>, <span class="fl" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">0.680</span>]</span>
<span id="cb4-11"></span>
<span id="cb4-12">curve <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">=</span> ql.DiscountCurve(dates, discounts, ql.Actual360())</span>
<span id="cb4-13">curve.enableExtrapolation()</span>
<span id="cb4-14"></span>
<span id="cb4-15"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Query the curve</span></span>
<span id="cb4-16"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">print</span>(<span class="ss" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">f"1Y discount  : </span><span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">{</span>curve<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">.</span>discount(today <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">+</span> ql.Period(<span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1</span>, ql.Years))<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">:.4f}</span><span class="ss" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"</span>)</span>
<span id="cb4-17"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">print</span>(<span class="ss" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">f"5Y discount  : </span><span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">{</span>curve<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">.</span>discount(today <span class="op" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">+</span> ql.Period(<span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">5</span>, ql.Years))<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">:.4f}</span><span class="ss" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"</span>)</span>
<span id="cb4-18"><span class="bu" style="color: null;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">print</span>(<span class="ss" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">f"10Y zero rate: </span><span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">{</span>curve<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">.</span>zeroRate(<span class="fl" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">10.0</span>, ql.Continuous)<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">.</span>rate()<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">:.4%}</span><span class="ss" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"</span>)</span></code></pre></div></div>
</section>
<section id="whats-next" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="whats-next">What’s next</h2>
<p>In the next post I’ll use this curve to price a vanilla interest rate swap — computing the fixed rate that makes the NPV zero at inception.</p>
